  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-10-10T15:57:57.646Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "'Use Low Latency' option of AVProVideo is removed since version 11.5.1, then our RTSP stream has massive 8 seconds latency (before update, it has 0.5 seconds latency).\nPlease don't update AVProVideo to 11.5.1 of VRChat client or contact them to revert the deletion of 'Use Low Latency' option.\nI'm providing TopazChat audio/video RTSP streaming service for VRChat musicians. We have a music live performance almost everyday. We implements it by AVProVideo and VRCSDK2 but recent AVProVideo update removed 'Use Low Latency' option, so our audio latency increased to 8 seconds from 0.5 seconds. Stream latency is crucial for us, that change will break our community.\nCurrently VRChat client uses AVProVideo version before 11.5.1, so existing worlds is fine. But we can't choose AVProVideo version on Unity Asset Store, so new world is affected by their changes.\nI opened the issue at AVProVideo GitHub relating this problem: https://github.com/RenderHeads/UnityPlugin-AVProVideo/issues/491",
